UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under IRC Section 2503(b), the annual gift tax exclusion applies only to gifts of present interests. Crummey withdrawal powers (per Crummey v. Commissioner, 397 F.2d 82) convert contributions to the ILIT into present interest gifts by granting each beneficiary a temporary withdrawal right. With 4 beneficiaries, the exclusion covers 4 × $19,000 = $76,000, and since the $40,000 premium is less than $76,000, the entire gift is excluded.
